{"type": "message", "id": "0155fa5c", "parentId": "aa40d7f8", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:17:32.206Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_f64eee4b0b5141d4ad9c429a", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"railway suicides decrease 2014 2020 percentage Spain Portugal Bulgaria Croatia Belgium France Germany UK Eurostat\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 948,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"949c71f1a56d5491\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"949c71f1a56d5491\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6804834f2caff03a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6804834f2caff03a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f9cd90c17c6ce1c7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU - European Commission\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f9cd90c17c6ce1c7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php/Rail_accident_fatalities_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"07f424c2582f49f9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWith 2 379 reported cases in 2018, ... ERA. ... The number of significant railway accidents fell between 2010 and 2018, with the exception of <strong>two increases in 2014 and 2017.</strong>...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"07f424c2582f49f9\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"27503df558c2a961\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSearch results for \\\"유로컵 참가국-（H87.CC）-유로컵 참가국->>h87.cc<<-h0neo.html\\\" - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"27503df558c2a961\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php/Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"837fcbfe24cc0be4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetrieved from &quot;https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Special:Search&quot;\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"837fcbfe24cc0be4\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f4c6b7675930f198\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRail transport fatalities drop by 11% in 2024 - News articles - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f4c6b7675930f198\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-eurostat-news/w/ddn-20251216-2\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4ce5d696188a75fb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>A decreasing trend was seen from 2014 to 2019, when the number fell by around 22%</strong>, and another sharp decrease of almost 15% compared with 2019 had been recorded by the end of 2021.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4ce5d696188a75fb\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 16, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"330d2040dbcfb4da\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"330d2040dbcfb4da\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c76f6059792c4476\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA total of 5 countries registered 4 or more deaths per thousand kilometres of railway tracks: <strong>Portugal (6.2), Hungary (5.8), Slovakia (5.7), Lithuania (4.6) and Poland (4.3).</strong> At the other end, 5 countries registered one or less fatality per thousand kilometres of railway tracks (Austria, Spain, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c76f6059792c4476\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"358aa7efde7c54fb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAssessment of the Impact of Rail Suicides on EU Railways\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"358aa7efde7c54fb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2022-10/Report%20on%20assessment%20of%20the%20impact%20of%20rail%20suicides%20on%20EU%20railways.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6f860ea4b50aadb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe European Union Agency for Railways (ERA) facilitates the development of the Single European Railway Area. It enhances interoperability, harmonises rules, and promotes safety. Since June 2019, ERA issues safety certificates and vehicle authorisations valid across multiple European countries.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6f860ea4b50aadb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.era.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7bb6fc548a829172\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEU railway deaths fall in 2024\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7bb6fc548a829172\\\">>>\",\n      \"u